(418, 1, '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '', 'Python programming', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'python-programming', '', '', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '', 107, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/section/python-programming/', 0, 'mto-section', '', 0),
(420, 1, '2022-01-12 04:46:54', '2022-01-12 04:46:54', '<p>In Python, condition statements act depending on whether a given condition is true or false. You can execute different blocks of codes depending on the outcome of a condition. Condition statements always evaluate to either True or False.In control statements, The <code>if</code> statement is the simplest form. It takes a condition and evaluates to either <code>True </code>or <code>False</code>.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">If the condition is <code>True</code>, then the True block of code will be executed, and if the condition is False, then the block of code is skipped, and The controller moves to the next line.</p>', 'Python Flow Control', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'python-flow-control', '', '', '2026-03-22 21:31:50', '2026-03-23 00:31:50', '', 418, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/lesson/python-flow-control/', 0, 'mto-lesson', '', 0),
